{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00409",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.58,
      "end_seconds": 7.24,
      "duration_seconds": 6.66,
      "text": "Hello there. Please, sit. What was the main thing you wanted to talk about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 8.43,
      "end_seconds": 15.99,
      "duration_seconds": 7.56,
      "text": "Honestly, it's pimples on my face, and my family pushed me to come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.61,
      "end_seconds": 18.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "When did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.48,
      "end_seconds": 26.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "It's been about three months now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.37,
      "end_seconds": 30.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "And how severe is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.33,
      "end_seconds": 33.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "Mostly moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.08,
      "end_seconds": 38.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.53,
      "end_seconds": 57.29,
      "duration_seconds": 17.76,
      "text": "It usually comes with dark marks after they heal. I mean, the dark marks after they heal? That's been for six months. There was flare-ups before my period, yes, but that went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.31,
      "end_seconds": 80.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.18,
      "end_seconds": 84.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "My father had a heart attack."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.73,
      "end_seconds": 87.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "What's your diet like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.18,
      "end_seconds": 92.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "I eat out quite a lot, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.43,
      "end_seconds": 95.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Do you get any exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.07,
      "end_seconds": 100.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "I walk for about half an hour most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.71,
      "end_seconds": 103.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Do you live alone?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.61,
      "end_seconds": 110.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Yes, I live on my own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.61,
      "end_seconds": 116.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "Tell me about your health in general, any ongoing conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.49,
      "end_seconds": 122.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "Yes, heart disease. I have heart failure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.32,
      "end_seconds": 127.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "Okay, I can see heart disease in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.29,
      "end_seconds": 141.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Which tablets or creams or inhalers do you use?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.77,
      "end_seconds": 159.37,
      "duration_seconds": 17.6,
      "text": "I mean, I take clopidogrel, 75 milligrams, once a day. Right, I take spironolactone, 25 milligrams, once a day for my heart. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.2,
      "end_seconds": 167.05,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "Have you ever reacted badly to a medicine or food? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.01,
      "end_seconds": 172.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "Yeah, uh, yes, eggs, it gives me a rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.09,
      "end_seconds": 179.82,
      "duration_seconds": 5.73,
      "text": "Have you noticed new face cream, irregular periods, pregnancy or excess hair growth?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.84,
      "end_seconds": 183.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "No, I'd have mentioned it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.01,
      "end_seconds": 188.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "How are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.97,
      "end_seconds": 190.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Nothing else aches."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.58,
      "end_seconds": 197.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "So, before we go on, a few quick readings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.42,
      "end_seconds": 206.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Rest your hand here..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.59,
      "end_seconds": 222.08,
      "duration_seconds": 5.49,
      "text": "Okay: temperature is 36.6 degrees, heart rate 69, pressure 110 over 70."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.87,
      "end_seconds": 225.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.25,
      "end_seconds": 230.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "I'll explain what that means shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.04,
      "end_seconds": 236.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "Right, let me check a few things physically."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.08,
      "end_seconds": 240.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Let me just check something."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.74,
      "end_seconds": 264.69,
      "duration_seconds": 6.95,
      "text": "There are red papules and a few pustules over the cheeks and chin, with some blackheads."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.0,
      "end_seconds": 269.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "That's fine, sit up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.0,
      "end_seconds": 284.34,
      "duration_seconds": 6.34,
      "text": "Having listened and examined, I'd lean towards moderate acne. I can't rule out rosacea yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 285.81,
      "end_seconds": 288.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Do you think it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.54,
      "end_seconds": 307.14,
      "duration_seconds": 17.6,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like moderate acne. I'm prescribing doxycycline, 100 milligrams, once a day, for six weeks. You take it by mouth. That's for acne. Don't squeeze them, that's how the marks stay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.61,
      "end_seconds": 324.2,
      "duration_seconds": 16.59,
      "text": "Hm, okay. It takes six to eight weeks to see the difference, so please don't give up in the first fortnight. Please don't wait if the symptoms get worse. That's when to be seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.76,
      "end_seconds": 328.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Alright, I know what to look for."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.84,
      "end_seconds": 339.45,
      "duration_seconds": 7.61,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in eight weeks. So, is there anything you wanted to ask?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 341.32,
      "end_seconds": 346.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "I think that's clear. Thank you for being so thorough."
    }
  ]
}